+### Compound Format
+
+Pass `compound: true` to break a duration into several parts. The output is compatible with Go's [`time.ParseDuration`](https://pkg.go.dev/time#ParseDuration): parts are glued together with no spaces, and hours are the largest unit (there is no `d`).
+
+```ts
+ms(5400000, { compound: true })       // "1h30m"
+ms(91800000, { compound: true })      // "25h30m"
+ms(-91800000, { compound: true })     // "-25h30m"
+ms(999, { compound: true })           // "0s"
+```
+
+Only hours, minutes and seconds are used, and leftover milliseconds are dropped. `compound` takes precedence over `long`. The output is meant for other tools to read, so `ms()` itself can't parse it back.
+
